menu "Gunshot classifier data link"

    config APP_DATA_LINK_USB_SERIAL_JTAG
        bool "Use native USB-Serial/JTAG for MFCC data link instead of UART0"
        default n
        help
            This board exposes two USB-C ports: one wired to the native
            USB-Serial/JTAG peripheral (used by esptool for flashing/monitor),
            and one wired to UART0 through a discrete USB-to-UART bridge chip.

            By default (n), the classifier data link (init_uart / the receive
            loop in main.cpp) uses the physical UART0 pins, matching the
            original wiring for a real deployment where a host talks to the
            board over that dedicated UART port.

            Enable this (y) to instead exchange MFCC data over the same native
            USB-Serial/JTAG port already used for flashing - convenient when
            only that port is connected (e.g. no separate UART-to-USB adapter
            wired up), such as during PC-vs-ESP32 validation.

endmenu
